{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Brave New World of the Internet"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Not That One!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Explain about technology and technical problems in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Discussing How to Deal with Problems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "One way to discuss how to deal with problems is to say what you would do if you were in someone else's situation. It is particularly useful if you want to discuss a complicated technical problem."}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you write an article about solving issues, you can use modals like <span class=\"italic\">would</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> should</span> or  <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to suggest solutions and offer assistance. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"italic\">I would ... </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I wouldn't ... </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">You could ... </span><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can also use must, might want to  or Imperatives to strongly suggest a solution."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"italic\">You might want to ... <br/> You must ...<br/> Always check ...</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are examples of Sally giving suggestions about how to deal with technical problems. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You must make sure that you check both the date of publication and the date of the last revision."}, {"type": "example", "content": "For this reason,  you should always cross-check the information found online."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You could also test the website's usability."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You might want to start by browsing the site."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You wouldn't want to waste your time on useless info!"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking About the Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>When you talk about a things that are not decided or when you make a  decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\"> will</span>.</li>  <li>When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\"> going to</span>.</li>  <li>When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or  booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.</li>  <li>When you talk about schedules or timetables in the future, you use the Simple Present tense</li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Verb Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Future Tense (Will)</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You won't have enough information on just one website for all your needs.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Old literary texts or philosophical works aren't going to change much in the future.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous Tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The next time you're doing research online, check the accuracy of the information.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present Tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> We expect the new generation of browsers to do that for us from next year onwards.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "up-to-date "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "containing the latest information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Not everything you read online is up-to-date."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le10ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you talk about the relevance of Internet websites."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "out of date"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " no longer valid or relevant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will find websites that are simply out of date."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le10ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flux"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a state of constant change"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Technology is in a constant state of flux"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le10ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cross-check"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to verify information by checking it against alternative sources"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should always cross-check your sources."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le10ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "usability"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the state of something being easy to use"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"